Package: supermox-dhcp-client
Architecture: all
Provides: isc-dhcp-client
Replaces: isc-dhcp-client
Conflicts: isc-dhcp-client
Depends: dhcpcd-base | udhcpc | busybox-udhcpc,
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: DHCP client adapter implementing the ISC dhclient contract
  SuperMox's answer to pve-container's dependency on isc-dhcp-client, which
  Devuan Ceres no longer ships (ISC DHCP is end-of-life upstream). It installs
  /sbin/dhclient as a POSIX sh adapter: it accepts the options pve-container's
  PVE::LXC::manage_dhclient and ifupdown2's dhcp method pass (-pf, -lf, -sf,
  -r, -s, -n, -q, -1, --timeout, --release, --renew, --request, interface
  names), obtains the binding from a maintained client that Devuan does ship
  (dhcpcd by default, udhcpc/udhcpc6 or a stand-in via SUPERMOX_DHCP_CLIENT),
  and translates it into the ISC dhclient-script contract the LXC hook
  consumes: reason, interface, new_ip_address, new_subnet_mask,
  new_network_mask, router_count, router_1..router_N, new_domain_name,
  new_domain_name_servers and pid, with every file written under $ROOTFS.
  It satisfies the "isc-dhcp-client" dependency of pve-container without
  copying any ISC source and without pulling in any systemd code.
